WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.980
BETH: Sometimes the challenging behaviour
of an individual with autism can become

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.140
so great that the family will need to
seek external support of specialists

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:12.369
to help and there are many different
sources of help and support available.

00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:16.780
If the distressed behaviour of a
child or family member presents a

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:21.180
significant risk to themselves or those
around them, specialist help should be

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.250
sought out to deal with the behaviour.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.799
JOE: They could request a social care
needs assessment for their family

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.860
member and for themselves as a carer.

00:00:30.619 --> 00:00:34.900
They may be able to get respite care
or the help of an outreach team who can

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.129
support them with behaviour strategies.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.030
Discussing this with a GP and
requesting a referral to a behavioural

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:42.930
specialist may be appropriate.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:48.110
Getting support from a counsellor who
understands autism and can support

00:00:48.139 --> 00:00:49.810
the individual and their family.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.169
BETH: There are a number of ways
in which a parent/carer can get

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:56.860
support such as meeting up with other
carers, getting ideas from other

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:00.960
families, and swapping tips in online
communities nationally or locally.

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:05.060
They could try contacting a
local ‘National Autistic Society’

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:09.160
group, community service or family
support service in their area.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:12.660
JOE: The ‘Challenging Behaviour
Foundation' has a lot of information

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:16.090
to help both parents and professionals
to give support and advice on

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:19.600
spotting behaviours that challenge
and what to do when it occurs.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:23.450
‘Scope' also has information for
parents on challenging behaviour.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:28.330
Families should not suffer in silence
as there is help out there and help

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:39.689
and support will make life better
for all concerned in the long run.

